\title{
Quantum $K$ theory for flag varieties and generalized Borel spaces
\author{I. Colombelli, E. Fatibene, M. Shaner}

This paper introduces the concept of quantum $K$-theories for certain types of algebraic varieties, specifically those related to flags. Building on a previous framework by Shiromano for classical and quantum Gromov-Witten theories of variety flags, our work expands this idea to groups and Borel pairs. We introduce the necessary mathematical definitions and formulas to describe the quantum Borel pair closed formula and introduce the bigdiagonal operator to describe the quantum Borel pair equality formula.

To illustrate our theory, we provide detailed descriptions and computations for the quantum Borel pair of the special linear group and its Borel pair, specifically looking at $SL(3,q)$ and its quantum Borel pair. Additionally, we introduce the idea of quantum Deligne-Mumford stacks and suggest directions for further research in this area.
